codex
The literature supports a distinction between square-root cancellation in each exponential sum and square-root fluctuations in the covering count. The former does not reach the required threshold through the usual discrepancy argument. I also verified that fixed linear families are Lehman-easy, so they do not obstruct a coverage-or-easy dichotomy; badly approximable ratios remain outside that escape.
